WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:06.819
Look, no matter what phase of your life you're
in right now, whether you're in the new, exciting

00:00:06.819 --> 00:00:10.269
phase, like the puppy love of a business or
relationship, or whatever you're doing, you're

00:00:10.269 --> 00:00:15.730
so excited about it, or in the steady phase,
or momentum phase, no matter where you're

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:21.760
at, at some point, you're going to hit a wall.
You're just going to. And when you hit a wall,

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:25.670
it is very interesting when a person hits
a wall because initially when you hit a wall,

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:30.151
you feel like everything is going to collapse.
You feel like everything's coming down. You

00:00:30.151 --> 00:00:34.079
feel like every single thing you are stressed
out about, you're worried about,. is going

00:00:34.079 --> 00:00:37.860
to collapse. It's almost like you feel it's
the end of life. It's like end of the world

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:44.400
is coming, right? And the way you behave and
react when you hit the wall creates a habit

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:48.410
in your life. And one of the worst habits,
there's a lot of people that say that the

00:00:48.410 --> 00:00:52.940
worst habit in their life is this and this
is the worst habit, I would tell you one of

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:57.700
the worst habits, if not the worst habit in
life is quitting. Quitting is a terrible habit

00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:01.219
to pick up because you're going to keep quitting
in your life. You'll keep quitting in your

00:01:01.219 --> 00:01:05.000
life and the next thing you know, every single
time you hit a wall, you'll quit.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:09.790
So, I have a system that I'm going to talk
to you about today, 10 different points why

00:01:09.790 --> 00:01:13.580
people quit and if you go through this, on
what you need to do for yourself, I'm going

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:17.290
through this right now, no matter what you're
going through right now in the quitting phase,

00:01:17.290 --> 00:01:20.270
there's something to do to overcome it. No
matter what you're going through right now.

00:01:20.270 --> 00:01:24.940
But before I even get into it, I want you
to even think about it in a complete different

00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:29.510
way. Think about how old you are right now.
I don't know how old you are right now. I

00:01:29.510 --> 00:01:35.270
want you to go back 10 years ago. If you're
30, you were 20. What were you worried about

00:01:35.270 --> 00:01:40.350
that was keeping you up at night at 20 years
old? 10 years ago. What were you worried about?

00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:44.000
What was keeping you up at night? Was it a
relationship, a girlfriend, at school a teacher,

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:49.950
professor, parent, argument, crisis, car payment,
tickets, suspension, DUI? What was it, 10

00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:56.400
years ago? Do you even worry about that today?
Was it the end of the world? No? The same

00:01:56.400 --> 00:02:01.440
thing is with business. Every single person
that builds a big business, at many different

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:07.060
points of their career have to slay some dragons.
You just have to slay some dragons. And the

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:11.340
better you go within time, the easier it gets
on slaying the next dragon.

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:12.820
So now let's talk about why people quit, 10
different reasons.

00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:17.750
#1: The number one reason why people quit
